{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he said, the officer</b> — It is the language of the Chaldeans: he who gives portions. And behold, the meaning of אשר מנה is like הפקיד (the appointee), and in the language of the Sages, ממונה. And since it derives from אשר מנה (who appointed), the divider of portions is very difficult, and all the more so since it is written about Daniel."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The comment addresses the grammatical form of המלצר (hameltzar); Ibn Ezra notes its Aramaic/Chaldean origin and the difficulty of deriving it from the root מנה."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:51.978183610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}